1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:05,420
One click creates one request. The app asks the database for a profile.

2
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:11,300
Fifty thousand people ask for the same profile. Repeated work makes the database the bottleneck.

3
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:17,500
Add a cache. The first lookup misses, reads the database, and saves the answer.

4
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:23,380
Next time, the lookup hits. Memory returns it in about one point one milliseconds, not four.

5
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:29,800
TTL expires old answers. Caching removes repeated work; the database still matters.
